{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form-if","title":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form-if","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1799,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:hypersurface-volume-form-if","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form-induced]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:induced-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-unit-normal-field]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:interior-multiplication]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form-if","line":2944,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Hypersurface Volume Form: the Sufficiency Half]\n\\label{prop:hypersurface-volume-form-if}\n\n\\uses{prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal, prop:hypersurface-volume-form-induced, def:induced-orientation, def:smooth-unit-normal-field, def:smooth-orientation, def:interior-multiplication}\n\n\n\n\nIf $n\\ge1$ and an isometric hypersurface immersion has a smooth global unit normal $N$, then $M$ is orientable and has a smooth orientation satisfying $dV_g=(N\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal,prop:hypersurface-volume-form-induced}\n\\sketch Use the smooth induced orientation from Proposition \\ref{prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal}; equation (2.17) is Proposition \\ref{prop:hypersurface-volume-form-induced}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Hypersurface Volume Form: the Sufficiency Half] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a6879706572737572666163652d766f6c756d652d666f726d2d6966\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahypersurface-orientable-of-normal\">↗ prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahypersurface-volume-form-induced\">↗ prop:hypersurface-volume-form-induced</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainduced-orientation\">↗ def:induced-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-unit-normal-field\">↗ def:smooth-unit-normal-field</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-orientation\">↗ def:smooth-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainterior-multiplication\">↗ def:interior-multiplication</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n\\ge 1$\">$n\\ge 1$</span> and an isometric hypersurface immersion has a smooth global unit normal <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N$\">$N$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is orientable and has a smooth orientation satisfying <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dV_g=(N\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M$\">$dV_g=(N\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink te